From b64f81edc0428d219e08521e5b6d662abca3dfbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 12:09:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Cast: Implement the device controller on the CastV2
 channel

Rework the device controller service so current Cast SDK clients can
connect and use a receiver:

- Clients that bind without a listener in the request extras (the
  connectionless client in current SDKs) add it through addListener and
  call connect(); the device is now connected and the result reported
  through onConnectedWithResult. The service advertises the
  cxless_client_minimal feature these calls require.
- Clients that pass their listener in the extras get the service
  request answered only once the device is connected (or with
  NETWORK_ERROR / AUTHENTICATION_FAILED if that fails).
- Requests for CAST_API (161) on the same action are answered with an
  ICastService implementation (feature flags, status code dictionary,
  integer maps; all empty) instead of failing the bind.
- Add the missing controller calls leaveApplication, requestStatus,
  setVolume, setMute and sendBinaryMessage, and the listener callbacks
  for leave/stop results, connection result and suspension. Transaction
  codes follow the Cast SDK's proxies.
- launchApplication honours LaunchOptions (relaunchIfRunning, language)
  and joinApplication joins the running session by application and
  session id instead of relaunching the application.
- Messages from the application are delivered for registered namespaces
  only, text and binary, including broadcasts; sendMessage reports
  success or failure with the namespace and request id, and rejects
  platform namespaces and payloads over 64 KiB.
- Receiver status updates are forwarded as device and application status,
  and application or connection loss is reported to the client.

CastChannelRegistry exposes the session of a connected device by device
id, e.g. for route volume changes.
